      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two issues in `lsm6dso_emul_init`:\n\n1. **Assertion failure when optional `int-gpios` is omitted**: `LSM6DSO_EMUL` (**line 293**) uses `GPIO_DT_SPEC_INST_GET_OR(inst, int_gpios, {})` and `lsm6dso_emul_set_interrupt_pin` (**line 67**) checks `if (config-\u003egpio_spec.port \u003d\u003d NULL)` because `int-gpios` is optional in `cros,lsm6dso-emul.yaml` (and omitted in existing devicetree overlays). When `int-gpios` is omitted, `config-\u003egpio_spec.dt_flags` is `0`, causing `__ASSERT(config-\u003egpio_spec.dt_flags \u0026 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, ...)` on line 273 to fail at init. Guard the assertion on `config-\u003egpio_spec.port !\u003d NULL`:\n   ```c\n   __ASSERT(config-\u003egpio_spec.port \u003d\u003d NULL ||\n   \t\t (config-\u003egpio_spec.dt_flags \u0026 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW) !\u003d 0,\n   \t \"The lsm6dso driver only supports active low configuration\");\n   ```\n   (And since active-low is enforced whenever `port !\u003d NULL`, lines 77–84 in `lsm6dso_emul_set_interrupt_pin` can also be simplified to `gpio_emul_input_set(config-\u003egpio_spec.port, config-\u003egpio_spec.pin, !active);`.)\n2. **Redundant `parent` assignment**: `data-\u003ei2c.i2c \u003d parent;` on line 269 is redundant because `.i2c \u003d DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_INST_PARENT(inst))` is already initialized statically in `LSM6DSO_EMUL` (**line 284**).\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/599ad52f-7519-45b2-a8a9-d96a1f962167)",
