      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] A few improvements to strengthen the test assertions and readability:\n\n1. **Missing sample value assertions in `test_gyro_sample` (lines 122–126)**: `test_gyro_sample` checks `sensor_num` and `flags`, but never verifies `data[count - 1].data[X]`, `data[count - 1].data[Y]`, or `data[count - 1].data[Z]`. If gyroscope data scaling or endianness is broken, the test will still pass.\n2. **Identical `0.0f` values for `y` and `z` mask axis-swap bugs (lines 45, 57, 76, 106, 116)**: Both tests pass `0.0f` for both `y` and `z`. Passing distinct non-zero values for all three axes (e.g., `(1.0f, 0.5f, -0.25f)` for accel and `(100.0f, 50.0f, -25.0f)` for gyro) ensures any swap between X, Y, and Z in `emul_lsm6dso_append_sample` or FIFO unpacking is caught:\n   ```c\n   emul_lsm6dso_append_sample(emul, MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_GYRO, 100.0f, 50.0f,\n   \t\t\t   -25.0f);\n   k_msleep(100);\n\n   count \u003d motion_sense_fifo_read(sizeof(data), ARRAY_SIZE(data), data,\n   \t\t\t       \u0026read_byte_count);\n   zassert_true(count \u003e\u003d 1, \"Expected at least 1 entry, got %d\", count);\n   zassert_equal(GYR_SENSOR_ID, data[count - 1].sensor_num);\n   zassert_equal(0, data[count - 1].flags);\n   zassert_within((100 * INT16_MAX) / gyr-\u003ecurrent_range,\n   \t       data[count - 1].data[X], 1);\n   zassert_within((50 * INT16_MAX) / gyr-\u003ecurrent_range,\n   \t       data[count - 1].data[Y], 1);\n   zassert_within((-25 * INT16_MAX) / gyr-\u003ecurrent_range,\n   \t       data[count - 1].data[Z], 1);\n   ```\n3. **Use named constants instead of raw literals (lines 36–37, 62, 81, 101–102, 122)**: Use `LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL` (from `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso_public.h`) instead of `13000`, and `ARRAY_SIZE(data)` instead of `4` in `motion_sense_fifo_read`.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/599ad52f-7519-45b2-a8a9-d96a1f962167)",
